                <pb facs="0842" n="748" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg748"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.30/111: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-10T16:00:00-05:00">September 10, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:44 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>199. Admiral Pye informs me that the junta desire to retain the services of
                    himself as well as Spears, Gunnell, and Compton. Davy’s contract, which was
                    shortly to expire, terminated by mutual agreement. He has been treated
                    generously by the junta. Wyatt’s contract will be canceled with 3 months’
                    pay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
